import './misses.css';
---
<figure class="miss-figure">
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 3</span>The lease ends before the old work does</div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="duration-chart">
   <div class="duration-scale"><span>0 ms</span><span>70 ms</span><span>140 ms</span></div>
   <div class="duration-row"><strong>A’s lease · 0–80 ms</strong><div class="duration-track"><span style="left:0;width:57.1429%"></span></div></div>
   <div class="duration-row"><strong>A’s source read · 0–120 ms</strong><div class="duration-track"><span class="work-bar" style="left:0;width:85.7143%"></span><i style="left:64.2857%;width:21.4286%"></i></div></div>
   <div class="duration-row"><strong>B’s source read · 90–140 ms</strong><div class="duration-track"><span class="work-bar" style="left:64.2857%;width:35.7143%"></span><i style="left:64.2857%;width:21.4286%"></i></div></div>
   <p>The outlined interval, 90–120 ms, contains two source reads.</p>
  </div>
  <ol class="trace">
   <li><time>0 ms</time><div><strong>App A owns P7’s lease: token α</strong><span>A begins a source read. The lease will expire at 80 ms.</span></div></li>
   <li><time>80 ms</time><div><strong>Token α expires; A is still running</strong><span>The store has forgotten the permission. Nothing has stopped A’s source read.</span></div></li>
   <li><time>90 ms</time><div><strong>App B acquires token β</strong><span>B starts another source read. Two reads now overlap for P7.</span></div></li>
   <li><time>120 ms</time><div><strong>A finishes and tries to publish with α</strong><span>The atomic owner check sees β and rejects A’s fill and release. B keeps its lease.</span></div></li>
   <li><time>140 ms</time><div><strong>B finishes while β is still valid</strong><span>B may publish only if the other freshness checks also pass.</span></div></li>
  </ol>
  <div class="lanes"><div class="lane"><div class="label">Source reads</div><div class="token" data-state="Running"><strong>A: 0–120 ms</strong><span>Continues beyond lease expiry</span></div><div class="token" data-state="Running"><strong>B: 90–140 ms</strong><span>Overlaps A for 30 ms</span></div></div><div class="lane"><div class="label">Cache publication</div><div class="token"><strong>A’s old token: refused</strong><span>Cannot overwrite through this guarded path</span></div><div class="token"><strong>B’s current token: eligible</strong><span>Ownership alone does not prove freshness</span></div></div></div>
 </div>
 <figcaption>An illustrative lease on one unchanged store, with unique owner tokens and an atomic check at each publication and release. Expiry, failover and lost coordination can allow duplicate source work; a lease is not a source concurrency limit.</figcaption>
</figure>
